{{Quote|It is imperative that this facility remain hidden and secure.|Emperor Palpatine, to Royce Hemlock|<ref name="SOT" />}}
'''Tantiss Base''', also identified as the '''Wayland facility''', was a clandestine scientific complex under the [[Galactic Empire]], built within [[Mount Tantiss]] on the [[planet]] [[Wayland]] in [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]]. Details of the facility operations were classified and its extant coordinates remained hidden.

After an [[Slither vine|incident]] on [[Setron]] during the early [[Imperial Era]], [[Doctor]] [[Royce Hemlock]] and the [[Advanced Science Division]] relocated to Tantiss Base and began development on [[Project Necromancer]], a secret [[Biologist|biological]] research project that involved [[Midi-chlorian|M-count]] transfer. Tantiss Base also maintained other top secret research and programs. 

In the aftermath of a raid by Clone Force 99 which resulted in Hemlock's [[death]], a [[Specimen A|Zillo Beast]] containment breach, and the subsequent uprising of the facility's clone prisoners, Tantiss Base sustained heavy damage with all research inside being destroyed. [[Governor]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] later ordered [[Captain]] [[Bragg]] to have the facility be closed indefinitely and redistributed its funds to [[Project Stardust]].

==Overview==
===Layout===
{{Quote|Emotion and sentiment have no place within these walls.|Royce Hemlock|<ref name="Confined" />}}
[[File:Advanced_Science_Division.png|left|thumb|270x270px|Chief Scientist Dr. Royce Hemlock oversaw the secret science and cloning facility.]]
Tantiss Base was a classified scientific installation utilized by the [[Galactic Empire]], located on two facilities: one on [[Mount Tantiss]],<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> codenamed Tantiss Base,<ref name="Confined" /> and the other on a neighboring [[mountain]], both in the [[planet]] [[Wayland]]. The Tantiss base consisted of two concentric rings comprised of multiple [[hangar]]s dug into the mountain, with ample space for landing ships in front of them as well as windows providing natural light to the interior of the base, and was surrounded by [[jungle]], which was home to dangerous creatures such as the [[dryax]]<ref name="SOT" /> while a [[river]] lay a short distance away.<ref name="Breach" /> The base was the headquarters of the [[Advanced Science Division]] and the final destination of scientists, experts and technology related to it and gathered from around the [[galaxy]].<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> Chief among them were lead [[Doctor]] [[Royce Hemlock]] who was in command of the facility's research division, his assistant [[Emerie Karr]] and former [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[clone commando]] [[Scorch]], the commander of the [[Imperial royal guard]]s stationed there. [[Kaminoan]] former chief cloning officer [[Nala Se]] was also imprisoned in the facility<ref name="Metamorphosis">{{TBB|Metamorphosis (episode)}}</ref> and provided her expertise in exchange for the [[genetically defective clone]] [[Omega]]'s safety.<ref name="Confined" />

===Access===
{{Quote|Any ship going there must first dock with Imperial Station 003, in orbit over Coruscant|Edmon Rampart explains how to locate Tantiss Base|<ref name="Breach" />}}
[[File:Imperial_orbital_station.png|right|thumb|240x240px|Imperial Station 003 was the only access for transports heading to Tantiss Base.]]
[[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] personally considered the facility and the experiments within to be one of the Empire's most important assets and stipulated that its location remain secret even among the Imperials themselves.<ref name="SOT" /> Coordinates for the planet were officially scrubbed from all transports heading there<ref name="Metamorphosis" /> while no mention of the system was held in archives off-site instead only referring to it by the [[sector]]'s name.<ref name="PU">{{TBB|Paths Unknown}}</ref> 

In order for a starship to even locate the base, it had to dock on [[Imperial Station 003]] on the Empire's [[capital]] planet [[Coruscant]], where it had its crew-including [[droid]]s and organics-inspected and the coordinates to Wayland transmitted to the [[navigation computer]] via direct link, ensuring that the crew<ref name="Breach">{{TBB|Into the Breach}}</ref> and even the [[officer]]s in command never learned of the planet's location themselves.<ref name="Juggernaut">{{TBB|Juggernaut (episode)}}</ref>

===Exterior fortifications===
{{Quote|It is far safer in here than out there.|Emerie Karr|<ref name="Confined" />}}
The facility was heavily guarded by the [[Imperial Military]], who enforced its exterior which included A number of [[turbolaser]] [[turret]]s were scattered around these rings to protect against airborne threats,<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> and several [[Alpha-3 Nimbus-class V-wing starfighter|V-wing starfighters]] from the [[Imperial Navy]] were on standby to intercept unauthorized craft entering the [[atmosphere]].<ref name="SOT" /> Should any infiltrators get past the aerial defenses, [[Low Altitude Assault Transport]]s were also stationed in the base to deploy search parties of [[TK stormtrooper]]s in the jungle to look for them.<ref name="Flash">{{TBB|Flash Strike}}</ref> In addition to these measures, to protect the base and its inhabitants against the planet's wildlife a perimeter was carefully maintained around the mountain by using trained [[lurca hound]]s to prevent any lifeforms from getting too close; any personnel wandering outside of it were considered to be lost.<ref name="Confined" />

===Interior facilities===
{{Quote|As you can see, the specimens are well-guarded to ensure they remain viable for testing.|Royce Hemlock, to Emperor Palpatine|<ref name="SOT" />}}
[[File:Mount_tantiss_containment_area.png|thumb|left|290px|The containment area of the main lab including cells for human and Zillo Beast subjects]]
Inside the base was a network of tunnels and rooms including a [[Prison|detention level]] where Nala Se and the other prisoners were held under guard from [[clone commando]]s,<ref name="Metamorphosis" /> a [[Tantiss Base communication center|communication center]],<ref name="Confined" /> and a [[Tantiss Base command center|command center]] from where the area around the prison and its essential functions could be monitored. The facility also included spartan cells for the former clone troopers used as test subjects by the program, including [[Crosshair]]. This clone prison was arranged in a cross-shape and being guarded by two [[TK stormtrooper]]s who monitored the prisoners from a central command console.<ref name="SOT" />

In order to carry out the purposes of the [[Imperial cloning program]], Tantiss Base included many research rooms and laboratories. A massive underground containment zone held multiple [[Cloning|clone]]d [[Zillo Beast]]s created by the cloning program and transported by [[science vessel]]s such as [[transport 904]], which were held in stasis for maximum protection.<ref name="Metamorphosis" /> One such Zillo Beast was experimented on using weaponry similar to that of the [[RX-200 Falchion-class assault tank|RX-200 ''Falchion''-class assault tank]].<ref name="Flash Strike">{{TBB|Flash Strike}}</ref> Nala Se also maintained a lab in the facility, which she used to experiment with the viability of clone blood to support an m-count. There were also stables for native lurca hounds, which were captured by the Imperials and tended to by Omega and the [[Unidentified Imperial labor droid|labor droid]] [[K-9X1]] to protect personnel stranded on the perimeter zone against the native wildlife,<ref name="Confined" /> or be unleashed against intruders wandering there. By far the most important and well-protected room in the mountain, however, was [[Tantiss vault|the Vault]]; a secure zone holding a number of reinforced tubes where the subjects the m-counts were sourced from were being kept. The entrance to the Vault was guarded by eight [[Imperial royal guard]]s and shielded by laser barriers to prevent unauthorized entrance.<ref name="SOT" /> The vault also included living quarters for [[Force-sensitive]] [[Youngling|children]] collected from around [[the galaxy]] by certain class one [[bounty hunter]]s and delivered to the Division for a price; they were tended to by [[Imperial nanny droid]]s and had their blood collected for testing on the daily by [[Tantiss medical droid]]s.<ref name="Identity" />

==History==
===Hidden experiments===
{{Quote|What he seeks is not possible.''"<br />"''Make it possible.|Nala Se and Royce Hemlock on the Emperor Palpatine's master plan|<ref name="Plan 99">{{TBB|Plan 99 (episode)}}</ref>}}
[[File:Blood_collection_room_weyland.png|left|thumb|240x240px|Experiments were performed on the clones of Tantiss Base]]
Soon after an [[Slither vine|incident]] in the [[Imperial medical laboratory|laboratory]] on [[Setron]], the [[Advanced Science Division]] relocated its headquarters to Tantiss Base on the planet Wayland.<ref name="PU" /> Following the Empire's [[Attack on Kamino]] which destroyed the [[Kaminoan]] facilities, the cloning technology and essential personnel were sent by [[Vice Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart]] by order of [[Governor]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] to Tantiss Base such as [[Chief Medical Scientist]] Doctor [[Nala Se]].<ref name="Lost">{{TBB|Kamino Lost}}</ref>

Blood tests were performed on retired [[clone trooper]]s held in the Base<ref name="SOT" /> to continue the search for midi-chlorian rich blood donors.<ref name="Harbinger">{{TBB|The Harbinger}}</ref> Hemlock<ref name="Bad">{{TBB|Bad Territory}}</ref> began capturing [[Force-sensitive]] subjects from around [[the galaxy]]<ref name="Harbinger" /> and had them delivered to Tantiss Base to be used for his experiments.<ref name="SOT" /> Other research performed at this time included development of the [[Zillo Beast]] clones,<ref name="Metamorphosis" /> the unlocking of the Kaminoans’ secrets,<ref name="SOT" /> and brainwashing clones for the Clone X division.<ref name="Infiltration">{{TBB|Infiltration (episode)}}</ref>

[[File:ProjectNecromancer.png|right|thumb|290px|Project Necromancer was considered to be of great importance to the future of the Empire.]]
[[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] made an unexpected visit to the secret facility to see the progress Doctors Hemlock and Se made on Project Necromancer. Hemlock gave him a tour of the site, including the Vault. Hemlock stated that with more time and resources, he was confident they have a successful M-count replication. Considering their work of great importance to the future of the Empire, Emperor Palpatine assured Hemlock that he would have whatever he required to accomplish Project Necromancer’s goal.<ref name="SOT" />

===Decommissioned===
{{Quote|Shutter this facility indefinitely and redistribute all funding to Project Stardust.|Tarkin to Bragg|<ref name="The Cavalry Has Arrived">{{TBB|The Cavalry Has Arrived}}</ref>}}
When Governor Tarkin’s fleet arrived to insistingly help end the attack on Tantiss Base, they found various wings of it sustaining heavy damage, Doctor Hemlock and several troopers of the Advanced Science Division dead and all of his research being non-salvageable since the databanks got destroyed by Se to keep Rampart from using Hemlock’s research as a bargaining chip to get his career in the Empire back and save her close friend [[Omega]]. Governor Tarkin believed Hemlock’s failures costed them enough and posthumously punished him by ordereing [[Captain]] [[Bragg]] to close Tantiss Base indefinitely and redistribute all funding and assets to [[Commander]] [[Orson Callan Krennic]]’s [[Project Stardust]].<ref name="The Cavalry Has Arrived">{{TBB|The Cavalry Has Arrived}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Weyland facility appeared in the [[August 13]], [[2021]] season one finale of the animated TV show ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'' named "[[Kamino Lost]],"<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> and was first identified by name in that episode's episode guide on StarWars.com, though the spelling did not match the planet's prior spelling.<ref name="KL EG" /> In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], [[Wayland/Legends|Wayland's]] [[Mount Tantiss/Legends|Mount Tantiss]] housed Emperor [[Palpatine/Legends|Palpatine's]] secret storehouses, including thousands of [[Spaarti cloning cylinder]]s.<ref name="The Last Command">''[[The Last Command]]''</ref>

